 (scope . "Repaired v1.00.30 W4 guarded compiled-root activation (issue #9690): .github/actions/prepare-racket-environment/action.yml, .github/actions/restore-racket-environment/action.yml, .github/actions/setup-racket/action.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml, scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt, scripts/ci/prepared-env-report.rkt, ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root-workflow.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt, tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt, artifacts/ci-recovery/v1.00.30-w4/** and artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w2/**, reviewed read-only against the frozen W4 wave doc in .planning/campaigns/96974d2cd97b152f99d296d6956f13b4f3b2bc4f79428894f74a1f3df49753d8/plan-snapshot/ and the BLOCKED-w4 repair list.")
 (report . "Round 3 review (independent, read-only VERIFY subagent) against implementation head f706e2c3799d3c2c37a3b2fcfaef041712274715 (content digest c7c51c6a68ae9dc378b4d7f9586156ab6650c636ea54d4556cad78e77543de53) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with four lane-wiring defects: (1) setup-racket's pre-resolution step used a hyphenated shell env var that parses as a shorter variable under set -u, so the activated path failed before resolution; (2) the lane expression publishes Q_CI_COMPILED_ROOT=auto, which both CLIs rejected (only off|verify|resolve were accepted), so an activated run would fail closed instead of resolving; (3) the fast-shard launch step passed only COMPILED_ROOT_FLAGS and never exported the lane switch, so the launcher ignored the resolved flags and every shard ran the no-flags current-source path; (4) the restore action's compiled-output loop materialized the verified root (q-compiled/trusted-root) into the checkout for every prepared-env consumer, exceeding the declared read-only scope. All four were reproduced and fixed, committed at f706e2c3799d3c2c37a3b2fcfaef041712274715: the resolution step now consumes a hyphen-free PREPARED_ENV_ROOT shell variable while its step output keeps the hyphenated name read by ci.yml; auto is an accepted resolution mode in scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt and ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root.rkt; the launch step exports Q_CI_COMPILED_ROOT from the job env; and the restore loop excludes q-compiled/trusted-root. The W2 dag-checkpoint was re-stamped for the changed setup action (action sha256, checkpoint hash, SHA256SUMS and the two pinned test literals). New committed tests cover the lane plumbing: the hyphen-free variable, auto vocabulary across both CLIs, the launch step env export, the restore exclusion, and a behavioral Q_CI_COMPILED_ROOT=auto run through the run CLI. The declared Verify chain is green at the head (167 focused tests, arch 32/32, security 64/64, workflows 33/33, check-deps OK, metrics --lint, fast 1208/1208) and retained at raw/verify-chain.txt. Round 4 review is solicited against this head; this entry is updated with that verdict and its narrative before the implementation pull request is merged. History: round 1 (independent review of the first repaired head) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with three blocking findings: the fast-env producer never passed the compiled-root input (so no consumer could ever hit the root), setup-racket's pre-resolution step invoked compiled-root run with no --module, which the CLI refused, and the branch carried a merge commit instead of a linear content history. All three were fixed and independently reproduced: the blocked head ce13d0388 has zero compiled-root input lines in ci.yml and fails the no-module run (raw/red-first-review-fixes.txt), and the history was flattened to single-parent content commits on fc1a6fa36. Round 2 returned REQUEST_CHANGES with five findings: the retained chain capture still showed a failed metrics lint (superseded by a green re-run on the resynced tree), the trio was still the stale blocked record (rebound here), the worktree branch was still named campaign/v1.00.30-w4-repair (renamed), setup-racket could touch a restored root without an explicit opt-in (the resolution step is gated on a resolution-mode input and ci.yml passes compiled-root-mode at the fast-shard call site), and the zero-module run behaviour had no committed test coverage (two CLI-level cases were added). The W2 checkpoint pins were re-stamped for the changed setup action. The wave's declared Verify chain is green end to end and retained at raw/verify-chain.txt."))